menu "Web server (web_server)"

    config WEB_SERVER_MAX_ROUTES
        int "Most API routes"
        default 32
        range 8 96
        help
            Routes registered with web_register(), the built-in ones included. Pages are
            served without a route each.

    config WEB_SERVER_MAX_SOCKETS
        int "Most open connections"
        default 7
        range 3 13
        help
            The server keeps three more sockets for itself: CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS must
            cover these, those three, and everything else the application opens.

    config WEB_SERVER_STACK_SIZE
        int "Server task stack"
        default 6144

    config WEB_SERVER_UPLOAD_STACK_SIZE
        int "Long-operation task stack"
        default 6144
        help
            An upload, a download, a copy or a scan runs on a task of its own, so the server
            keeps answering (web_job_run()).

    config WEB_SERVER_PULL_STACK_SIZE
        int "Download task stack"
        default 8192
        help
            A pull runs on a task of its own. TLS wants most of it.

    config WEB_SERVER_CORS_ORIGINS
        string "Sites whose pages may call the API (CORS), space-separated"
        default ""
        help
            Origins -- scheme://host[:port] -- allowed to call the API from a browser: an API
            tool such as https://editor.swagger.io, or a project's documentation site.
            https://*.example.com allows every subdomain of example.com (not example.com
            itself: list both). `*` allows any site. Empty: none but the board's own pages.
            `web cors` on the console changes the list, kept in NVS; `web cors reset` comes
            back to this one. An allowed site can drive the board unless a password is set.

    config WEB_SERVER_CORS_MAX_LEN
        int "Most characters in the CORS list"
        default 384
        range 64 1024

endmenu
